 A plain-text resume system where all content lives in a single YAML file and
 outputs are generated programmatically. Edit once, publish everywhere.
 
+## Neuroengineering update October 2026
+
+The canonical resume now leads with current UC Davis M.S. enrollment, human
+single-unit analysis, 128-channel DeepArray/Intan bench work, experiment timing,
+and recorded-data validation of AI-assisted software. Acquisition integration,
+streaming interpretation, and adaptive semantic screening are described at their
+current stage of development.
+
+- [Experience inventory and active goals](resume/career/experience_inventory.md)
+  records completed work, ongoing projects, evidence, and scope for future agents.
+- [Role targeting and employer requirements](resume/career/target_roles.md)
+  explains the strongest job families, current gaps, and primary employer sources.
+- `neuroengineering`, `neural_data`, and `acquisition_validation` generate
+  research-first resumes and corresponding letter variants. Existing analytics
+  and clinical profiles remain available.
+
+Run build commands from the `resume/` directory. Generated application drafts are
+in [resume/career/drafts](resume/career/drafts); edit YAML and rebuild before
+customizing a draft for a particular opening. Keep future work in the inventory
+until an implementation or measurement supports an accomplishment claim.
+
+```bash
+cd resume
+python scripts/build_resume.py --profile neural_data --md-only
+python scripts/build_resume.py --profile acquisition_validation --md-only
+python scripts/build_cover_letter.py --company "Company Name" --role "Research Engineer" --profile neuroengineering --md-only
+```
+
+Profiles support `research_first`, `max_bullets_per_research_role`, and an ordered
+`project_names` list. An empty project list suppresses neuroscience projects for
+an unrelated application. Cover-letter `profile_overrides` select evidence
+appropriate to each role.
+
 ---
 
 ## Why YAML as the source of truth
