+
+Re: Acquisition and Test Engineer — Neurotechnology Team
+
+I am applying for the Acquisition and Test Engineer position at Neurotechnology Team. I bring hands-on neural acquisition bench testing in Dr. Jie Zheng's lab at UC Davis, a Biomedical Engineering M.S. focus in neuroengineering, and professional experience in laboratory quality control and technical operations. I am particularly interested in acquisition integration, troubleshooting, and test engineering.
+
+I co-led bench testing of a 128-channel DeepArray/Intan setup, mapping probe and RHX channels and investigating grounding, filter behavior, shorts, and high-impedance channels. Our lab testing identified 121 channels with clean test-signal recordings. I also work on PsychoPy/RHX event synchronization using TCP annotations and Cedrus C-Pod TTL markers, with measurements of clock drift and event-alignment residuals.
+
+My analysis work connects sorted neural data and event markers to PSTHs, allowing me to check whether repeated responses are recovered through the pipeline. I also develop Python configuration, launch, and diagnostic tooling for Neuralynx/Dark Horse Neuro workflows, with recording and replay validation still in progress.
+
+I use AI coding agents to accelerate implementation and check the results against recorded signals, timing measurements, and repeatable responses. This gives me concrete ways to investigate whether a pipeline preserves the experimental information it is intended to measure.
+
+Earlier work at Eurofins Test America developed my laboratory documentation and quality-control habits. At First Step Communities, I build data workflows and support technical systems across multiple sites, translating operational requirements into tools colleagues can use.
+
+I would welcome a discussion of how my acquisition, analysis, and validation experience could support your team. Thank you for your consideration.
+
+Sincerely,
+
+Marco Del Fava
