+# Marco Del Fava
+
+mdelfava@ucdavis.edu | 707-637-6544 | Sacramento, CA
+
+[GitHub](https://github.com/BarkBarkBarkBarkBarkBarkBark) | [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/marc-del-fava) | [Portfolio](https://transformations.solutions)
+
+
+## Summary
+
+Biomedical Engineering M.S. student at UC Davis working on human single-unit electrophysiology, neural acquisition, and Python analysis pipelines. Experience spans Intan/DeepArray bench testing, Neuralynx and Dark Horse Neuro workflows, spike sorting, experiment synchronization, and event-aligned response analysis. Develops tools with AI coding agents and evaluates outputs against recorded signals, timing measurements, and reproducible neural responses.
+
+## Research and Volunteer Experience
+
+**Research Volunteer — UC Davis Health — Z-Lab (Dr. Jie Zheng)** | Sacramento, CA | Jul 2025 – Present
+
+- Process human microwire recordings with SpikeInterface, MountainSort5, Kilosort4, and O-Sort; compare Neuralynx CSC and MED-derived inputs to investigate conversion precision and spike-detection discrepancies.
+- Develop experiment synchronization with PsychoPy, Intan RHX TCP annotations, and Cedrus C-Pod TTL markers; measured clock drift and event-alignment residuals to assess timing limitations.
+- Co-led bench testing of a 128-channel DeepArray/Intan acquisition setup; mapped probe and RHX channels and investigated grounding, filter behavior, shorts, and high-impedance channels. Lab testing identified 121 of 128 channels with clean test-signal recordings.
+- Built a Python workflow combining sorted single-unit data and event markers to generate PSTHs for repeated 30-second stories; reproduced an event-associated response in the same unit across six repetitions.
+
+**Research Volunteer — UC Davis Health — Neuroscience Unit E5** | Sacramento, CA | Dec 2022 – Jul 2023
+
+- Prepared headboxes and EEG application kits for the Epilepsy Monitoring Unit.
+- Shadowed EEG technologists and observed clinical neurophysiology procedures for patients with epilepsy and traumatic brain injury.
+
+
+
+## Selected Projects
+
+**Semantic Neuron simulation** | 2026
+
+- Built a NEURON prototype linking sentence-embedding cosine similarity to stochastic synaptic input in a Hodgkin-Huxley compartment with fixed synaptic weights.
+- Implemented seeded trials and outputs for membrane voltage, presynaptic and postsynaptic spike times, and firing rates to explore semantic-tuning hypotheses in simulation.
+- Links: [GitHub](https://github.com/BarkBarkBarkBarkBarkBarkBark/semantic_neuron)
+
+
+**Dark Horse Neuro / Neuralynx acquisition pipeline** | 2026
+
+- Develop Python orchestration for DHN-AQ configuration, SSH launch, acquisition diagnostics, and Neuralynx Pegasus/NetCom integration.
+- Implemented RC/CS configuration writers and an NRD-to-UDP replay prototype; hardware reception and recording validation remain in progress.
+- Links: [GitHub](https://github.com/BarkBarkBarkBarkBarkBarkBark/dhn_client) · [Docs](https://barkbarkbarkbarkbarkbarkbark.github.io/dhn_client/)
+
+
+## Experience
+
+**Operations Specialist — First Step Communities** | Sacramento, CA | Jul 2021 – Present
+
+- Analyzed program and partner datasets using Python, SPSS, and Excel to identify predictors of successful exits and service effectiveness.
+- Maintain multi-site IT systems, network segmentation, and camera/NVR integrations; troubleshoot device connectivity and document workflows for nontechnical staff.
+
+**Analyst — Eurofins Test America** | West Sacramento, CA | Oct 2019 – Jun 2021
+
+- Maintained high-accuracy data entry and review in a regulated laboratory environment; supported QA documentation and adherence to standard operating procedures.
+- Performed solvent extraction of organic compounds from soil and water samples in a high-throughput production setting.
+
+## Education
+
+**M.S. Biomedical Engineering** | University of California, Davis | Sep 2026 - Present
+
+Neuroengineering track; research in Dr. Jie Zheng's Z-Lab
+
+**M.S. Psychology (GPA: 3.7)** | Arizona State University | 2023
+
+**B.S. Neuroscience, Physiology, and Behavior** | University of California, Davis | 2017
+
+
+## Skills
+
+**Neural Data & Signal Processing:** Human intracranial recordings and Behnke-Fried microwire data, Spike sorting (SpikeInterface, MountainSort5, Kilosort4, O-Sort), Preprocessing and waveform analysis, Event alignment and peri-stimulus time histograms (PSTHs)
+
+**Neural Acquisition & Tooling:** Intan RHX and 128-channel DeepArray bench testing, Neuralynx CSC/NEV data and Pegasus/NetCom workflows, Dark Horse Neuro acquisition and MED conversion workflows, PsychoPy/TCP event integration and Cedrus C-Pod TTL markers, Channel mapping, grounding, and signal-quality troubleshooting
+
+**Scientific Software & Modeling:** Python (NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, Neo), MATLAB and AWS GPU sorting workflows, NEURON and semantic embedding prototypes, Git, Linux, and shell scripting
+
+**Software Validation & Reproducibility:** AI-assisted scientific software development, Recorded-data comparisons and repeatable response checks, Clock-drift and event-timing analysis, Synthetic signal and simulation-based prototyping
+
+
+## Certifications
+
+- **Data Analysis with Matplotlib, Pandas, and Scikit-Learn Python Libraries** — UC Davis Continuing and Professional Education (2025-09-18) — [View badge](https://www.credly.com/badges/505ef11c-58b4-48bd-aa9e-5a21f0247d46/public_url)
+- CITI — Biomedical Research
+- CITI — Essentials of Research Administration
+- CITI — GCP Social and Behavioral Research Best Practices
